From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HarmonyOS Porting <porting@harmonyos.org>
Date: Fri, 27 Mar 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 21/21] Makefile.pre.in: use HARDLINK for libpython.so
 development symlink on HarmonyOS

On HarmonyOS, HMDFS does not properly track symbolic links.
os.path.exists() returns False for symlinks, and the dynamic linker
(ld.lld) cannot find shared libraries through symlinks.

This causes pip install to fail for all C extension packages, because
the linker reports "unable to find library -lpython3.12" when searching
through the libpython3.12.so -> libpython3.12.so.1.0 symlink.

Fix: Change $(LN_FORCE) to $(HARDLINK) (cp -p on HarmonyOS) when creating
the libpython$(LDVERSION).so link during make install altbininstall.
This creates a real file copy that HMDFS can track properly.

Note: This patch must be applied AFTER patch 0004, which introduces
$(LN_FORCE) for this line. Only the LDLIBRARY link is changed; other
symlinks in altbininstall (e.g., python executable) correctly use
$(LN_FORCE) as set by patch 0004.

The trade-off is ~10MB extra disk space (copying libpython3.12.so.1.0),
but this is necessary for C extension compilation to work.

Adapted from Python 3.9 port patch 0024.
---
 Makefile.pre.in | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Makefile.pre.in b/Makefile.pre.in
--- a/Makefile.pre.in
+++ b/Makefile.pre.in
@@ -1994,7 +1994,7 @@
 			else \
 				$(INSTALL_SHARED) $(LDLIBRARY) $(DESTDIR)$(LIBDIR)/$(INSTSONAME); \
 				if test $(LDLIBRARY) != $(INSTSONAME); then \
-					(cd $(DESTDIR)$(LIBDIR); rm -f $(LDLIBRARY); $(LN_FORCE) $(INSTSONAME) $(LDLIBRARY)) \
+					(cd $(DESTDIR)$(LIBDIR); rm -f $(LDLIBRARY); $(HARDLINK) $(INSTSONAME) $(LDLIBRARY)) \
 				fi \
 			fi; \
 			if test -n "$(PY3LIBRARY)"; then \
